          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ढोलक — ḍholak — \"a small two-headed drum\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "शादी में औरतें ढोलक बजाकर गाती हैं। Śādī meṁ aurteṁ ḍholak bajākar gātī haiṁ. At weddings the women play the dholak and sing."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ढोलक (ḍholak) is a tadbhava, inherited from Sanskrit ḍhōla, \"a drum\" (CDIAL 5608)."
            }
          ]
        },
